X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2486339-virtual-event-can-we-trust-ai-inside-the"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:VIRTUAL EVENT: Can We Trust AI? Inside the Government's Approach t
 o Implementing Responsible AI for National Security
DTSTART:20261202T180000Z
DTEND:20261202T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261116T144758Z
UID:20261202T180000Z-2486339@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261202T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/135/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2000,2000/31509_GLOBAL_COMPETENCIES_SKILLS_DEVELOPMENT_SE
 RIES.rev.1784660853.png
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,T
 raining, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:AI is transforming how government organizations access informa
 tion\, analyze data\, and make decisions. But successfully adopting AI\, p
 articularly in national security\, requires more than technology.  Drawing
  on his experience supporting the Department of War's War Data Platform\, 
 David Kalishman will explore how government organizations are putting resp
 onsible AI governance into practice through three foundational pillars:Pol
 icy: Establishing standards\, governance frameworks\, and accountability. 
    Process: Turning governance principles into repeatable practices that e
 nable secure and scalable AI adoption.    People: Building the leadership\
 , workforce capabilities\, and organizational culture needed to sustain ad
 option and trust.      The session will also introduce the publicly availa
 ble CDAO Responsible AI Toolkit as a real-world example of operationalizin
 g responsible AI principles. To make the session interactive\, students wi
 ll participate in a short hands-on exercise evaluating a hypothetical gove
 rnment AI use case\, identifying risks\, and recommending safeguards befor
 e deployment.Key Takeaways for Students:AI Governance &amp\; National Secu
 rity: Balancing innovation\, security\, accountability\, and operational e
 ffectiveness.    Beyond Technology: Understanding how Policy\, Process\, a
 nd People enable responsible AI adoption at scale.    Interdisciplinary Le
 adership: How professionals in public policy\, international affairs\, and
  technology can shape the future of AI governance.    Format: 45-minute pr
 esentation followed by a 15-minute Q&amp\;A.Speaker BioDavid Kalishman is 
 a Senior Manager at Accenture\, supporting the Department of War's War Dat
 a Platform\, a major initiative focused on advancing enterprise data acces
 sibility\, artificial intelligence\, and data-driven decision-making acros
 s the defense enterprise.  His work focuses on strengthening Data and AI G
 overnance through three interconnected pillars: Policy\, Process\, and Peo
 ple. This includes establishing governance structures\, operational proces
 ses\, and organizational capabilities that accelerate AI adoption while ma
 intaining security\, accountability\, and responsible oversight. Working a
 t the intersection of technology\, strategy\, and national security\, Davi
 d focuses on translating emerging AI capabilities into practical and safe 
 implementation approaches. He is also an alumnus of the Hacking for Defens
 e (H4D) community. Meeting URL: https://iu.zoom.us/my/hlspesp
LAST-MODIFIED:20261116T200303Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2486339-virtual-event-can-we-trust-ai-
 inside-the
