X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 45": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2488599-the-actors-volume-information-session"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_45
SUMMARY:The Actors Volume Information Session
DTSTART:20261202T230000Z
DTEND:20261203T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261118T162114Z
UID:20261202T230000Z-2488604@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261202T230000Z
CATEGORIES:Career development
DESCRIPTION:The Actors Volume is a videogame community and podcast focused
  on providing industry insights and exploring the craft behind great games
 . Co-founders Jeff Berg (PCAP and voice actor\, 12 years in the industry) 
 and Matthew Brezina (mocap assistant director and producer\, 7 years in th
 e industry) met while shooting Dragon Age: The Veilguard. Matthew and Lydi
 a Smyth\, our Director of Social Media Strategy\, are both 2016 graduates 
 of the IU Media School.  On the show\, we sit down with top creatives in t
 he game industry\, including actors\, directors\, casting directors and pr
 oducers\, to talk about the craft behind their work and the paths that got
  them where they are\, so others can follow.  In a session with Game Desig
 n students\, we'd love to give students who want to work in games the chan
 ce to ask working professionals how AAA performance capture shoots come to
 gether\, hear the many ways people find their way into the industry\, and 
 get answers about building a career in games.  We'd also like to introduce
  our remote internships for Media School students (Producer\, Editor and S
 ocial Media Writer)\, which offer hands-on experience alongside working in
 dustry professionals.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T212114Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2488599-the-actors-volume-informatio
 n-session
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Actors Volume is a videogame communi
 ty and podcast focused on providing industry insights and exploring the cr
 aft behind great games. Co-founders Jeff Berg (PCAP and voice actor\, 12 y
 ears in the industry) and Matthew Brezina (mocap assistant director and pr
 oducer\, 7 years in the industry) met while shooting Dragon Age: The Veilg
 uard. Matthew and Lydia Smyth\, our Director of Social Media Strategy\, ar
 e both 2016 graduates of the IU Media School.</p><p>  On the show\, we sit
  down with top creatives in the game industry\, including actors\, directo
 rs\, casting directors and producers\, to talk about the craft behind thei
 r work and the paths that got them where they are\, so others can follow.<
 /p><p>  In a session with Game Design students\, we'd love to give student
 s who want to work in games the chance to ask working professionals how AA
 A performance capture shoots come together\, hear the many ways people fin
 d their way into the industry\, and get answers about building a career in
  games.</p><p>  We'd also like to introduce our remote internships for Med
 ia School students (Producer\, Editor and Social Media Writer)\, which off
 er hands-on experience alongside working industry professionals.</p>
