X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Interactive Frequencies II: A Multimedia Concert
DTSTART:20261203T233000Z
DTEND:20261204T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261117T145226Z
UID:20261203T233000Z-2487407@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261203T233000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,733,495/33577_InteractiveFreqII_Image.rev.1794851394.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art, music, films, and performances,Art and museum exhibitions,
 Community events,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a sensorial evening featuring time-based works dev
 eloped through a collaboration between Eskenazi School's Interactive Art c
 ourse and the Jacobs School's Music Performance &amp\; Media course. Worki
 ng with Jiji Kim\, Associate Professor of Guitar\, and Megan Young\, Senio
 r Lecturer of Digital Art\, students develop contemporary compositions in 
 a range of musical and visual styles. The evening also features a special 
 screening of&#160\;ResursiveBodies\,&#160\;an interdisciplinary project su
 pport by the KIX Lab and created by Dance\, Theater\, and Art faculty. Tog
 ether\, these works explore connections between sound\, image\, and human 
 experience\, informed by guest lecturers on heart rate tracking and public
  health outcomes.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261117T195226Z
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, 525 East 9th Street\, Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2486300-interactive-frequencies-ii-a
 -multimedia-concert
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us for a sensorial evening featurin
 g time-based works developed through a collaboration between Eskenazi Scho
 ol's Interactive Art course and the Jacobs School's Music Performance &amp
 \; Media course. Working with Jiji Kim\, Associate Professor of Guitar\, a
 nd Megan Young\, Senior Lecturer of Digital Art\, students develop contemp
 orary compositions in a range of musical and visual styles. The evening al
 so features a special screening of&#160\;<em>Resursive</em><em>Bodies\,&#1
 60\;</em>an interdisciplinary project support by the KIX Lab and created b
 y Dance\, Theater\, and Art faculty. Together\, these works explore connec
 tions between sound\, image\, and human experience\, informed by guest lec
 turers on heart rate tracking and public health outcomes.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>Jiji Kim<br />\nAssociate Professor of Music<b
 r />\njk319@iu.edu</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2487407
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,733\,495/33577_InteractiveFreqII_Image.rev.1
 794851394.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>Enjoy an interactive\, multi-media performance at t
 he McCalla Center!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:Academics|Arts and Humanities|Community engagement
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
