SUMMARY: Writers Guild Prose Reading with Nate Powell
DESCRIPTION:The Writers Guild is thrilled to host award-winning graphic n
 ovelist Nate Powell for our December 6 First Sunday Prose Reading Series.
  PLEASE NOTE: NEW LOCATION: REDBUD BOOKS at 408 W. Kirkwood Avenue https:
 //www.google.com/maps/search/408+W.+Kirkwood+Avenue?entry=gmail&source=g 
 . Nate will read a portion of his newest work\, Diana\, a prequel to his 
 last graphic novel\, Fall Through. Images from Diana will be up on screen
 . Audience members may purchase his books at this event.\n\nNate Powell i
 s a National Book Award-winning cartoonist who began self-publishing comi
 cs as an Arkansas teenager in 1992.\n\nHis work includes the new graphic 
 novel Diana\, a prequel to his last book\, Fall Through\, and a comics ad
 aptation of James Loewen’s Lies My Teacher Told Me\, as well as Save It F
 or Later\, civil rights icon John Lewis’ March trilogy and its follow-up 
 Run\, viral comics essay About Face\, and graphic novels Come Again\, Two
  Dead\, Any Empire\, and Swallow Me Whole. He has published nonfiction co
 mics and written for The Washington Post\, The Nib\, Popula\, Booklist\, 
 CNN\, and The Weather Channel.\n\nPowell’s work has also received a Rober
 t F. Kennedy Book Award\, multiple Eisner and Ignatz Awards\, ALA and YAL
 SA distinctions\, the Comic-Con International Inkpot Award\, and the CXC 
 Transformative Work Award. He has discussed his work at the United Nation
 s\, as well as on MSNBC’s The Rachel Maddow Show\, CNN\, NPR\, PBS\, and 
 Free Speech TV.\n\nFrom 1992 to 2010\, he performed and toured in multipl
 e underground punk bands including Soophie Nun Squad and Universe\, and m
 anaged DIY label Harlan Records.
CATEGORIES:Free,Literary-Arts,In-Person
