X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:ACES Horizon Talk: "Spring Fever in the Gobi: Labor\, Economy\, an
 d Care in Cashmere Harvest Interactions" by Dr. Kathryn Graber
DTSTART:20261209T173000Z
DTEND:20261209T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261118T145350Z
UID:20261209T173000Z-2488473@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261209T173000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/176/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1545,2000/33575_ACES_Horizon_Talk_Graber.rev.1794847696.p
 ng
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:The Association of Central Eurasian Students (ACES) warmly inv
 ites you to our upcoming Horizon Talk\, featuring Dr. Kathryn Graber. Join
  us for an engaging discussion titled "Spring Fever in the Gobi: Labor\, E
 conomy\, and Care in Cashmere Harvest Interactions."  &#160\;  In Mongolia
 's rural herding economy\, it is difficult to overstate the importance of 
 the spring cashmere harvest. For most herding families\, cashmere is the m
 ain source of cash income for the year. So before their goats begin to nat
 urally shed\, herders quickly comb them\, capturing the valuable undercoat
  from millions of animals nation-wide over a few feverish weeks.  Combing 
 sessions are about more than extraction\, however. This talk examines huma
 n-goat and human-human interactions during combing sessions in the Gobi to
  show what else is achieved in these moments: sharing labor\, aligning per
 ception\, working out property relations\, and caring for both the animals
  and each other.  &#160\;  Sponsored by: Central Eurasian Studies (CEUS) a
 nd the Inner Asian and Uralic National Resource Center (IAUNRC).  &#160\; 
  Please note that this event will be in person only. There will not be a Z
 oom or hybrid option. Lunch will be provided.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T195350Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2486253-aces-horizon-talk-spring-fev
 er-in-the-gobi-labor
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">  The A
 ssociation of Central Eurasian Students (ACES) warmly invites you to our u
 pcoming Horizon Talk\, featuring <strong>Dr. Kathryn Graber</strong>. Join
  us for an engaging discussion titled <strong>"Spring Fever in the Gobi: L
 abor\, Economy\, and Care in Cashmere Harvest Interactions."</strong></p><
 p>  &#160\;</p><p data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">  In Mongolia's rural
  herding economy\, it is difficult to overstate the importance of the spri
 ng cashmere harvest. For most herding families\, cashmere is the main sour
 ce of cash income for the year. So before their goats begin to naturally s
 hed\, herders quickly comb them\, capturing the valuable undercoat from mi
 llions of animals nation-wide over a few feverish weeks.</p><p>  Combing s
 essions are about more than extraction\, however. This talk examines human
 -goat and human-human interactions during combing sessions in the Gobi to 
 show what else is achieved in these moments: sharing labor\, aligning perc
 eption\, working out property relations\, and caring for both the animals 
 and each other.</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>  Sponsored by: Central Eurasian Stu
 dies (CEUS) and the Inner Asian and Uralic National Resource Center (IAUNR
 C).</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>  Please note that this event will be in person 
 only. There will not be a Zoom or hybrid option. Lunch will be provided.</
 p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2488473
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/176/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1545\,2000/33575_ACES_Horizon_Talk_Graber.re
 v.1794847696.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:ACES Horizon Talk: <span data-olk-copy-source="M
 essageBody">"Spring Fever in the Gobi: Labor\, Economy\, and Care in Cashm
 ere Harvest Interactions" by</span> Dr. Kathryn Graber
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Dr. Kathryn Graber will give her talk on&#160\;
 "Spring Fever in the Gobi: Labor\, Economy\, and Care in Cashmere Harvest 
 Interactions" <span data-preserver-spaces="true">on December 9th</span> <s
 pan data-preserver-spaces="true">at 12:30 PM in GISB Room 2134.</span>\n</
 p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
