X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Eskenazi School of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344752-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-am-session", "Architecture + Design": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344752-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-am-session", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2344752-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-am-session"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344752-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-am-session"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Light and Chemistry (AM Session)
DTSTART:20261210T150000Z
DTEND:20261210T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T121537Z
UID:20261210T150000Z-2352813@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261210T150000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1081,1081/31448_HSD-FullColor.rev.1783430812.png
DESCRIPTION:Through hands-on experiments with viewfinders\, pinhole camera
 s\, and cyanotype photograms\, students will discover how photography can 
 document history\, reflect change\, and draw inspiration from nature. From
  framing a scene to harnessing the power of sunlight\, we'll investigate h
 ow images are made and what they can communicate. Join us to experiment\, 
 observe\, and create your own light-powered photographs!  Program designed
  by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12.Know Before You 
 Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the m
 useum at 10 am. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before exploring 
 the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll
  head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterp
 ieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperone
  required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for ever
 y 6 children.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260716T161537Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344752-homeschool-day-light-and-che
 mistry-am-session
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Through hands-on experiments with viewfi
 nders\, pinhole cameras\, and cyanotype photograms\, students will discove
 r how photography can document history\, reflect change\, and draw inspira
 tion from nature. From framing a scene to harnessing the power of sunlight
 \, we'll investigate how images are made and what they can communicate. Jo
 in us to experiment\, observe\, and create your own light-powered photogra
 phs!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in
  grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us i
 n the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 10 am
 . Together\, we'll drop off personal items before exploring the galleries.
  After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to 
 the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't f
 orget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. <strong>Chaperon
 e required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adul
 t for every 6 children.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Madelyn Cage</strong><br />\n  You
 th and Family Art Education Manager<br />\n  Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Muse
 um of Art<br />\n  <a href="mailto:cagem@iu.edu">cagem@iu.edu<br />\n  812
 -855-0607</a>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2352813
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1081\,1081/31448_HSD-FullColor.rev.178343081
 2.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Homeschool Day graphic
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Explore how artists use light to capture images
  and tell stories about the world around them.&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:Architecture + Design, Eskenazi Museum of Art, IU Eskenazi School of Art
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 237": "https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2376647-hivsti-testing"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_237
SUMMARY:HIV/STI Testing
DTSTART:20261210T150000Z
DTEND:20261210T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260810T150649Z
UID:20261126T150000Z-2376647@events.iu.edu__20261210
DESCRIPTION:Free HIV Testing &amp\; Safer Sex Supplies at the LGBTQ+ Cultu
 re Center  Taking care of your sexual health is an important part of your 
 overall well-being\, and we're committed to making resources accessible\, 
 welcoming\, and judgment-free.Positive Link (https://iuhealth.org/find-med
 ical-services/positive-link-hiv-services) provides free and confidential H
 IV testing in Room 204 of the LGBTQ+ Culture Center every Thursday from 10
 :00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. during the academic year. During the summer\, testin
 g is available on the first and third Thursdays of each month.  In additio
 n\, during the academic year\, the Monroe County Health Department offers 
 free chlamydia and gonorrhea testing on the third Thursday of every month\
 , also from 10:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. in Room 101.  The LGBTQ+ Culture Cente
 r also offers a variety of free safer sex supplies\, including condoms\, i
 nternal condoms\, dental dams\, lubricants\, and educational materials on 
 proper use. These resources are available to all students\, free of charge
 . You can find them in the kitchenette area near the back entrance of the 
 Center and are welcome to take what you need.  STI Testing &amp\; Safer Se
 x Resources Beyond Campus  Prioritizing your sexual health should be simpl
 e and accessible. In addition to services available at the LGBTQ+ Culture 
 Center\, students can receive testing on campus through the IU Student Hea
 lth Center (https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/medical/sti-testing/index.htm
 l) or visit several local organizations (https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/
 health-answers/sexual-health/sti-testing-resources.html) that offer free o
 r low-cost testing and prevention services.  Many of these providers offer
  confidential care\, safer sex supplies\, and supportive information about
  prevention\, treatment\, and sexual wellness. If you're unsure where to s
 tart\, we're happy to help connect you with resources that fit your needs.
 All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultur
 al\, and historical observances welcome all members of the Indiana Univers
 ity community.
GEO:39.168722;-86.525274
LAST-MODIFIED:20260818T140215Z
LOCATION:LGBTQ+ CULTURE CENTER
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2376647-hivsti-testing
