DTSTART:20261210T223000Z
DTEND:20261211T003000Z
LOCATION:IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology\, 416 N. Indiana Ave.\
 , Bloomington\, IN 47408
GEO:39.170023;-86.526132
SUMMARY:Winter at the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Event Details:&#160\;  Get out of the cold and cozy up for a 
 night of winter wonder! Join the IUMAA for Winter at the Museum\, a festi
 ve evening filled with a flurry of creativity and imagination.Decorate wr
 eaths\, ornaments\, and dreidels while surrounded by delicate harp melodi
 es.  Thinking of loved ones far away? Decorate your own holiday card to s
 end their way!  Want to add some flair to your own home festivities? Make
  some beaded garlands and decorate your own ornaments.    Don't forget to
  enjoy some hot chocolate and holiday pastries!  This program is free and
  open to all\, with Museum galleries remaining open for the duration of t
 he event to give a special\, after-hours view of the exhibitions.Parking 
 Information:  Limited complimentary parking is available in front of the 
 Museum entrance (https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA) off Indiana A
 venue. Free street parking is available in surrounding neighborhoods on w
 eekends and weekdays after 5:00 PM.  Paid parking is also available in th
 e University Collections at McCalla (https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCA
 CruHA) parking lot off Indiana Avenue and the Indiana Memorial Union (htt
 ps://maps.app.goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA) visitor lot.  Metered street park
 ing is also available near Sample Gates and throughout downtown Bloomingt
 on\, including along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Street\
 , North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.Quest
 ions?  For accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, pleas
 e reach out to Camden Hill at camrhill@iu.edu (mailto:camrhill@iu.edu) or
  (812) 855-1696.Note:  By attending this event\, you agree to be in photo
 graphy that may be used by the University for promotional purposes. If yo
 u would not like to be in any pictures\, please speak to a Museum staff m
 ember and they will inform assigned photographers of your request. If you
  see that your image has been used in error\, please reach out to iumaa@i
 u.edu (mailto:iumaa@iu.edu) to request that it be taken down.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Event Details:</strong>&#160\;</p
 ><p>  Get out of the cold and cozy up for a night of winter wonder! Join 
 the IUMAA for Winter at the Museum\, a festive evening filled with a flur
 ry of creativity and imagination.</p><ul><li>Decorate wreaths\, ornaments
 \, and dreidels while surrounded by delicate harp melodies.  </li><li>Thi
 nking of loved ones far away? Decorate your own holiday card to send thei
 r way!  </li><li>Want to add some flair to your own home festivities? Mak
 e some beaded garlands and decorate your own ornaments.  </li></ul><p>  D
 on't forget to enjoy some hot chocolate and holiday pastries!</p><p>  Thi
 s program is free and open to all\, with Museum galleries remaining open 
 for the duration of the event to give a special\, after-hours view of the
  exhibitions.</p><p><strong>Parking Information:</strong></p><p data-pm-s
 lice="1 1 []">  Limited complimentary parking is available in front of th
 e <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA">Museum entrance</a>
  off Indiana Avenue. Free street parking is available in surrounding neig
 hborhoods on weekends and weekdays after 5:00 PM.</p><p data-pm-slice="1 
 1 []">  Paid parking is also available in the <a href="https://maps.app.g
 oo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCACruHA">University Collections at McCalla</a> parking lo
 t off Indiana Avenue and the <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78
 o5twJA">Indiana Memorial Union</a> visitor lot.</p><p data-pm-slice="1 1 
 []">  Metered street parking is also available near Sample Gates and thro
 ughout downtown Bloomington\, including along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th 
 Street\, East 4th Street\, North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and
  South Grant Street.</p><p><strong>Questions?</strong></p><p>  For access
 ibility assistance or questions about this event\, please reach out to Ca
 mden Hill at <a href="mailto:camrhill@iu.edu">camrhill@iu.edu</a> or (812
 ) 855-1696.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong></p><p>  By attending this event\
 , you agree to be in photography that may be used by the University for p
 romotional purposes. If you would not like to be in any pictures\, please
  speak to a Museum staff member and they will inform assigned photographe
 rs of your request. If you see that your image has been used in error\, p
 lease reach out to <a href="mailto:iumaa@iu.edu">iumaa@iu.edu</a> to requ
 est that it be taken down.</p>
