SUMMARY:Happiness 2.0 mask workshop – Dec. 11
DTSTART:20261211T150000Z
DTEND:20261211T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20260826T110343Z
UID:20261211T150000Z-2396832@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261211T150000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/45/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,600,600/32208_red-mask-parallax.rev.1787754693.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Health and wellness,Training, non-cr
 edit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the fall semester\, Indiana University undergraduat
 e and high school students from the Bloomington community are invited to p
 articipate in the Happiness 2.0 Mask Workshops — an interactive experien
 ce that brings together science\, art\, and reflection on digital life.  T
 he experience combines three components:an accessible discussion of curren
 t research on digital media and identity  a guided exploration of artworks
  in the Eskenazi Museum's galleries  a hands-on mask-making activity    Dr
 awing inspiration from both the research discussion and the museum experie
 nce\, participants will create a mask representing aspects of their own di
 gital identity and experiences with digital media. Topics explored through
 out the workshop include identity formation\, online self-presentation\, t
 he relationship between online and offline selves\, and well-being.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T205229Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/mediaiub/event/2396832-happiness-20-mask-worksho
 p-dec-11
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Throughout the fa
 ll semester\, Indiana University undergraduate and high school students fr
 om the Bloomington community are invited to participate in the Happiness 2
 .0 Mask Workshops — an interactive experience that brings together scien
 ce\, art\, and reflection on digital life.</p><p>  The experience combines
  three components:</p><ul><li>an accessible discussion of current research
  on digital media and identity  </li><li>a guided exploration of artworks 
 in the Eskenazi Museum's galleries  </li><li>a hands-on mask-making activi
 ty  </li></ul><p>  Drawing inspiration from both the research discussion a
 nd the museum experience\, participants will create a mask representing as
 pects of their own digital identity and experiences with digital media. To
 pics explored throughout the workshop include identity formation\, online 
 self-presentation\, the relationship between online and offline selves\, a
 nd well-being.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">\n  Laura Marciano<br /
 >\n  <a href="mailto:laumarci@iu.edu">laumarci@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2396832
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/45/width/168/height
 /168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,600\,600/32208_red-mask-parallax.rev.17877546
 93.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Red paintbrush marking a white mask
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">\n  Undergraduate and high s
 chool students are invited to participate in this interactive workshop.\n<
 /p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Media School
END:VEVENT
