X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Knobstone Hiking Trail Association Of Indiana Meetup": "https://www.meetup.com/knobstone-hiking-trail-association-of-indiana-meetup/events/rbmvztyjcqbqb/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_knobstone_hiking_trail_association_of_indiana_meetup
X-SOURCE:Knobstone Hiking Trail Association
UID:event_rbmvztyjcqbqb@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064828Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261212T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261212T153000
SUMMARY:2nd Weekend Work Day Trail Building
DESCRIPTION:Knobstone Hiking Trail Association of Indiana Meetup\nWould yo
 u like to spend a day in some beautiful woods with a delightful group of p
 eople building a connecting section of Indiana’s premier long distance h
 iking trail? Come join us as we continue work on the Tecumseh Trail extens
 ion portion of the KHT in MMSF. We will be building the new trail includin
 g clipping green briar.\nPlease bring a lunch and water. We will have larg
 e hand tools\, but please bring any small tools you have such as clippers 
 or a pruning saw. And a backpack is handy to carry everything in. Instruct
 ions will be provided for those who need them. We finish about 3:30.\nMeet
  at the parking lot at the base of Gose Creek Road at the end of Hinson Ro
 ad in Martinsville.\nJoin us on our website at http://www.knobstonehikingt
 rail.org/\, on Facebook at [www.facebook.com/groups/2255586117953484](http
 ://www.facebook.com/groups/2255586117953484)\, and Substack [https://khta.
 substack.com/](https://khta.substack.com/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/knobstone-hiking-trail-association-of
 -indiana-meetup/events/rbmvztyjcqbqb/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260820T230542Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260820T230542Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_48ac7e6a73bd950b28dea0eca41b3050858f0c4f00ddfbd78dd23a2a9e5fc51d
SUMMARY:Daughters of the King - Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261212T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261212T120000
DTSTAMP:20261121T064845Z
UID:l4ln9iarv0kk179p6hq9m7v12r@google.com__20261212
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20250310T211808Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><br>Daughters of the King “DOK” is a world-wide religio
 us order founded in 1885 by Episcopal women. Today it includes women from 
 a wide variety of Christian traditions. Members of the DOK are ordinary wo
 men who are married and single\, live in the world\, and dedicate themselv
 es prayer\, service and evangelism. Monthly gatherings include educational
  programs\; recent programs at Trinity have highlighted Amish communities 
 of faith\, virtual prayer retreats\, handling conflict\, book reviews\, th
 e Lenten season\, Mary Magdalene\, and many other topics related to Christ
 ian faith and life. Members help with church events throughout the year.</
 p><p>Trinity’s chapter usually meets on the <strong>2nd Monday of the m
 onth at 5:00 pm</strong> in the Church Library\; check the announcements 
 in the Sunday worship bulletin for any change in location. All women inter
 ested in loving service and spiritual fellowship are welcome. For more inf
 ormation contact the Rev. Virginia Hall at <a href="mailto:yesvirginia194
 2@gmail.com">yesvirginia1942@gmail.com</a> or Heather Lake at <a href="m
 ailto:hr42lake@gmail.com">hr42lake@gmail.com</a>.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261119T142232Z
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library - Southwest Branch\, 865 S Lora Batc
 helor Dr\, Bloomington\, IN 47403\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Trinity Episcopal Church
END:VEVENT
