DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261224
DTSTAMP:20261118T152909Z
UID:20261204T220000Z-2488551@events.iu.edu__20261223
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/72/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,1080,1350/33600_2026_Exhibit_Instagram_Post_Graphic_1_1.re
 v.1795022863.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:IUPAI proudly presents our newest exhibition "Behind Gray Wall
 s\," showcasing students' artwork and writing produced over the last year.
  Our opening reception is on December 4th from 5-8 pm during Gallery Walk.
   Larissa Danielle taught two visual art courses\, both in the summers of 
 2025 and 2026 respectively. We will feature 6 physical paintings from her 
 latest class!  Kenny Mitchell taught a creative writing course in Spring 2
 026. Three original works written by his students will be presented throug
 h a listening booth separate from the art exhibit.  Monetary donations wil
 l be accepted at the opening reception. A talk will be given by IUPAI's Pr
 ogram Coordinator\, David Bandera. Food and drink will be provided! Be sur
 e to attend and offer your support!
GEO:39.16705;-86.524718
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T202909Z
LOCATION:MAXWELL HALL
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2488422-beyond-gray-walls-an-iu-pris
 on-arts-student
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  IUPAI proudly presents our newest exhibi
 tion "Behind Gray Walls\," showcasing students' artwork and writing produc
 ed over the last year. Our opening reception is on December 4th from 5-8 p
 m during Gallery Walk.</p><p>  Larissa Danielle taught two visual art cour
 ses\, both in the summers of 2025 and 2026 respectively. We will feature 6
  physical paintings from her latest class!</p><p>  Kenny Mitchell taught a
  creative writing course in Spring 2026. Three original works written by h
 is students will be presented through a listening booth separate from the 
 art exhibit.</p><p>  Monetary donations will be accepted at the opening re
 ception. A talk will be given by IUPAI's Program Coordinator\, David Bande
 ra. Food and drink will be provided! Be sure to attend and offer your supp
 ort!</p>
