ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,768/33570_segerman_henry_osuma-square-768x768.rev.1794
 617101.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:This symposium&#160\;seeks to redefine the genre of mathematic
 al art\, welcome an international cohort of its practitioners\, and identi
 fy IUB as a leading site for interdisciplinary dialogue between mathematic
 s and the arts.  Organized by Eskenazi School Associate Professor of Inter
 ior Design Jiangmei Wu\, who also curated the exhibition\, and Professor o
 f Mathematics Kevin Pilgrim\, the symposium starts Friday\, January 15 at 
 noon and continues through Saturday afternoon.  Over three keynotes\, them
 atic panels\, and workshops\, participating artists\, designers\, mathemat
 icians\, and scholars will explore mathematics as an active medium of crea
 tive practice and create a shared space for exchange among disciplines.Vis
 it here for more information about the exhibition. (https://eskenazi.india
 na.edu/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium.html)V
 isit here for the symposium schedule. (https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/events
 /special-events/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium-symposium.html)This projec
 t was supported by Indiana University's Presidential Arts and Humanities P
 rogram\; the Office for Research Development\, Indiana University Research
 \; and also at Indiana University Bloomington: Eskenazi School of Art\, Ar
 chitecture + Design\; Department of Mathematics\; and Luddy School of Info
 rmatics\, Computing and Engineering Artificial Intelligence Center (LAIC).
LAST-MODIFIED:20261113T232853Z
LOCATION:Four locations on the Bloomington campus
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2484592-mathematics-as-a-medium-a
 rt-practice-and-inquiry-
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This symposium&#160\;seeks to redefine t
 he genre of mathematical art\, welcome an international cohort of its prac
 titioners\, and identify IUB as a leading site for interdisciplinary dialo
 gue between mathematics and the arts.</p><p class="p1">  Organized by Eske
 nazi School Associate Professor of Interior Design Jiangmei Wu\, who also 
 curated the exhibition\, and Professor of Mathematics Kevin Pilgrim\, the 
 symposium starts Friday\, January 15 at noon and continues through Saturda
 y afternoon.</p><p class="p1">  Over three keynotes\, thematic panels\, an
 d workshops\, participating artists\, designers\, mathematicians\, and sch
 olars will explore mathematics as an active medium of creative practice an
 d create a shared space for exchange among disciplines.</p><p class="p1"><
 a href="https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/upcoming
 /2027-01-15-math-medium.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit here fo
 r more information about the exhibition.</a></p><p class="p1"><a href="htt
 ps://eskenazi.indiana.edu/events/special-events/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-m
 edium-symposium.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit here for the sy
 mposium schedule.</a></p><p class="p1"><em>This project was supported by I
 ndiana University's Presidential Arts and Humanities Program\; the Office 
 for Research Development\, Indiana University Research\; and also at India
 na University Bloomington: Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design\
 ; Department of Mathematics\; and Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing 
 and Engineering Artificial Intelligence Center (LAIC).</em></p>
