ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/135/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,400,400/33597_peace_corps_logo.rev.1795014681.jpg
CATEGORIES:Career development,Culture and languages,Lectures, talks, semin
 ars, and conferences,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunit
 ies
DESCRIPTION:Tired of the usual career tracks and ready to actually make a 
 tangible difference on the ground?  Join the HLS Office of Policy Engageme
 nt and Strategic Partnerships and Peace Corps Regional Recruiter Claudale 
 Daniels for an interactive\, zero-BS virtual info session and Q&amp\;A. Fo
 rget traditional desk jobs—we're talking about on-the-ground immersion w
 here you learn a new language\, integrate into a local community\, and tac
 kle real-world challenges side-by-side with global partners.  Whether you'
 re passionate about international development\, education\, environmental 
 action\, or public service\, we'll break down:The Real Experience: What da
 ily life\, cultural integration\, and grassroots collaboration actually lo
 ok like in the field.    Choose Your Path: Exploring traditional 2-year gl
 obal service\, flexible Peace Corps Response projects\, and the Virtual Se
 rvice Pilot.    The Long Game: How stepping into the world post-graduation
  builds the kind of cross-cultural leadership\, grit\, and global network 
 that sets you apart in any career—plus paths like the Coverdale Fellowsh
 ip and federal career benefits.      Bring your questions\, grab your coff
 ee\, and find out how to take your global ambitions off the screen and int
 o the real world before Claudale visits IU's campus in person later this s
 pring! Meeting URL: https://iu.zoom.us/my/hlspesp
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T160519Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2488302-level-up-your-global-impact-pe
 ace-corps-virtual
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="10">  Tired o
 f the usual career tracks and ready to actually make a tangible difference
  on the ground?</p><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="11">  Join the HLS Offi
 ce of Policy Engagement and Strategic Partnerships and Peace Corps Regiona
 l Recruiter Claudale Daniels for an interactive\, zero-BS virtual info ses
 sion and Q&amp\;A. Forget traditional desk jobs—we're talking about on-t
 he-ground immersion where you learn a new language\, integrate into a loca
 l community\, and tackle real-world challenges side-by-side with global pa
 rtners.</p><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="12">  Whether you're passionate
  about international development\, education\, environmental action\, or p
 ublic service\, we'll break down:</p><ul dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="13">
 <li><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="13\,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="1
 3\,0\,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Real Experience:</strong> What daily l
 ife\, cultural integration\, and grassroots collaboration actually look li
 ke in the field.    </p></li><li><p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="13\,1\,0"
 ><strong data-path-to-node="13\,1\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Choose Your P
 ath:</strong> Exploring traditional 2-year global service\, flexible Peace
  Corps Response projects\, and the Virtual Service Pilot.    </p></li><li>
 <p dir="ltr" data-path-to-node="13\,2\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="13\,2
 \,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Long Game:</strong> How stepping into the 
 world post-graduation builds the kind of cross-cultural leadership\, grit\
 , and global network that sets you apart in any career—plus paths like t
 he Coverdale Fellowship and federal career benefits.    </p></li></ul><p d
 ir="ltr" data-path-to-node="14">  Bring your questions\, grab your coffee\
 , and find out how to take your global ambitions off the screen and into t
 he real world before Claudale visits IU's campus in person later this spri
 ng!</p> Meeting URL: https://iu.zoom.us/my/hlspesp
