SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: White House Situati
 on Room to Big Tech - Career Dinner w/ Belinda Jackson Farrier & Shelby Sm
 ith-Wilson
DTSTART:20270217T223000Z
DTEND:20270218T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260723T164831Z
UID:20270217T223000Z-2358956@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20270217T223000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/135/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2000,2000/31509_GLOBAL_COMPETENCIES_SKILLS_DEVELOPMENT_SE
 RIES.rev.1784660853.png
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,T
 raining, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Cold messages on LinkedIn rarely lead to meaningful career bre
 akthroughs. This session gives you direct\, unscripted access to two senio
 r executives whose careers bridge the highest levels of international dipl
 omacy\, national security\, and Silicon Valley leadership.  Feel free to d
 rop in as your schedule allows and stay for as long as your evening permit
 s. You do not need to attend the full duration to participate\, grab dinne
 r\, and engage with our guests.  Who You Will Meet  You will connect direc
 tly with two former Senior Foreign Service officers and global executive l
 eaders:A Former Director for Global Rapid Response at Google (YouTube Trus
 t &amp\; Safety): A career diplomat who served in the White House Situatio
 n Room and the State Department Operations Center before transitioning to 
 top tier tech leadership.    A Senior Government Executive &amp\; Diplomat
  across 5 Countries: An expert in crisis management\, strategic negotiatio
 ns\, and executive leadership who prepares senior officials for high stake
 s global environments.      Together\, they also co-host the Leadership Te
 a Podcast and run their own executive advisory firms.  Value for Every Deg
 ree LevelUndergraduate Students: Learn how to break into competitive secto
 rs like foreign policy\, national security\, and tech strategy directly fr
 om women who held those roles.    Master Students: Get realistic strategie
 s for translating government and public policy tradecraft into high value 
 roles in corporate policy\, tech\, and consulting.    PhD Candidates: Lear
 n how to compress complex academic research into punchy executive briefs t
 hat cabinet secretaries and C-suite leaders actually read.      Key Discus
 sion TopicsWriting Under Pressure: Mastering Bottom Line Up Front framewor
 ks for high level decision makers.    The Government to Tech Pivot: Moving
  from government operations to senior roles in Silicon Valley.    Crisis L
 eadership: Managing teams and making critical decisions when information i
 s limited and stakes are high.      Speaker ProfilesBelinda Jackson Farrie
 r  Belinda Jackson Farrier is the Founder of Sweetgrass Advisory Group and
  co-host of the Leadership Tea Podcast. She served as a career member of t
 he Senior Foreign Service with the U.S. Department of State\, holding post
 ings in Rwanda\, El Salvador\, Togo\, and Peru. In Washington\, her assign
 ments included the State Department Operations Center\, the White House Si
 tuation Room\, and the Washington Foreign Press Center. She later joined G
 oogle\, where she served as Director for Global Rapid Response in YouTube 
 Trust and Safety.Shelby Smith-Wilson  Shelby Smith-Wilson is the Founder o
 f The FendAll Collaborative and co-host of the Leadership Tea Podcast. A s
 enior government executive\, diplomat\, and leadership strategist\, her gl
 obal career spans five countries. She specializes in change and crisis man
 agement\, strategic negotiation\, and cross-cultural leadership\, advising
  senior executives on guiding organizations through complex structural tra
 nsitions and high stakes disruptions.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260810T184714Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2358956-global-competencies-skills-dev
 elopment-series-white-
