 er\, and engage with our guests.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="13">  Who You W
 ill Meet</h4><p data-path-to-node="14">  You will connect directly with tw
 o former Senior Foreign Service officers and global executive leaders:</p>
 <ul data-path-to-node="15"><li><p data-path-to-node="15\,0\,0"><strong dat
 a-path-to-node="15\,0\,0" data-index-in-node="0">A Former Director for Glo
 bal Rapid Response at Google (YouTube Trust &amp\; Safety):</strong> A car
 eer diplomat who served in the White House Situation Room and the State De
 partment Operations Center before transitioning to top tier tech leadershi
 p.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="15\,1\,0"><strong data-path-to-no
 de="15\,1\,0" data-index-in-node="0">A Senior Government Executive &amp\; 
 Diplomat across 5 Countries:</strong> An expert in crisis management\, str
 ategic negotiations\, and executive leadership who prepares senior officia
 ls for high stakes global environments.    </p></li></ul><p data-path-to-n
 ode="16">  Together\, they also co-host the <i data-path-to-node="16" data
 -index-in-node="32">Leadership Tea Podcast</i> and run their own executive
  advisory firms.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Value for Every Degree Le
 vel</h4><ul data-path-to-node="18"><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,0\,0"><st
 rong data-path-to-node="18\,0\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Undergraduate Stu
 dents:</strong> Learn how to break into competitive sectors like foreign p
 olicy\, national security\, and tech strategy directly from women who held
  those roles.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,1\,0"><strong data
 -path-to-node="18\,1\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Master Students:</strong> 
 Get realistic strategies for translating government and public policy trad
 ecraft into high value roles in corporate policy\, tech\, and consulting. 
    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,2\,0"><strong data-path-to-node=
 "18\,2\,0" data-index-in-node="0">PhD Candidates:</strong> Learn how to co
 mpress complex academic research into punchy executive briefs that cabinet
  secretaries and C-suite leaders actually read.    </p></li></ul><h4 data-
 path-to-node="19">  Key Discussion Topics</h4><ul data-path-to-node="20"><
