 ode="0">Crisis Leadership:</strong> Managing teams and making critical dec
 isions when information is limited and stakes are high.    </p></li></ul><
 h3 data-path-to-node="22">  Speaker Profiles</h3><p data-path-to-node="23"
 ><strong data-path-to-node="23" data-index-in-node="0">Belinda Jackson Far
 rier</strong></p><p data-path-to-node="24">  Belinda Jackson Farrier is th
 e Founder of Sweetgrass Advisory Group and co-host of the <i data-path-to-
 node="24" data-index-in-node="87">Leadership Tea Podcast</i>. She served a
 s a career member of the Senior Foreign Service with the U.S. Department o
 f State\, holding postings in Rwanda\, El Salvador\, Togo\, and Peru. In W
 ashington\, her assignments included the State Department Operations Cente
 r\, the White House Situation Room\, and the Washington Foreign Press Cent
 er. She later joined Google\, where she served as Director for Global Rapi
 d Response in YouTube Trust and Safety.</p><p data-path-to-node="25"><stro
 ng data-path-to-node="25" data-index-in-node="0">Shelby Smith-Wilson</stro
 ng></p><p data-path-to-node="26">  Shelby Smith-Wilson is the Founder of T
 he FendAll Collaborative and co-host of the <i data-path-to-node="26" data
 -index-in-node="83">Leadership Tea Podcast</i>. A senior government execut
 ive\, diplomat\, and leadership strategist\, her global career spans five 
 countries. She specializes in change and crisis management\, strategic neg
 otiation\, and cross-cultural leadership\, advising senior executives on g
 uiding organizations through complex structural transitions and high stake
 s disruptions.</p>
